<title>INDIA: India oil pool gap seen rising to 245 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>India oil pool gap seen rising to 245 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India has said its oil pool account would be in deficit by 245 billion rupees by March 31, 1998, up from a shortfall of 155 billion one year earlier, unless steps were taken to contain it.</p>
<p>Petroleum Minister T.R. Balu told the lower house of parliament that the amount represented outstanding dues payable to the oil companies by the government.</p>
<p>&quot;Government is exploring various options to contain this deficit,&quot; he said in a written reply to a lawmaker's question released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Balu said the net oil import bill for the 1996/97 fiscal year ended on March 31 totalled $9.32 billion, well above an earlier estimate of $7.34 billion. ($1=35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
